---
/** How much per week, and why the summit sits well above 150 minutes. Rendered by /science/movement/weekly-volume; see scienceTopics.ts. */
import SplitCard from "../../components/science/SplitCard.astro";
import CitationCard from "../../components/CitationCard.astro";
import VideoSlot from "../../components/VideoSlot.astro";
import {
  WEEKLY_VOLUME_SECTION,
} from "../../data/science";
---

<SplitCard eyebrow="In the app" wide>
  <p>
    The Activity page draws your week as a climb, with flags at 150, 300
    and 560 minutes. The line is your aerobic minutes; the flags are where
    the evidence below changes what it says.
  </p>
  <svg slot="panel" viewBox="0 0 248 104" class="block h-auto w-full" aria-hidden="true">
    <line x1="0" y1="88" x2="248" y2="88" stroke="rgba(255,255,255,0.08)" />
    <polygon fill="rgba(52,211,153,0.12)" points="6,86 54,72 100,58 148,40 196,26 232,18 232,86" />
    <polyline fill="none" stroke="#34d399" stroke-width="2.2" points="6,86 54,72 100,58 148,40 196,26 232,18" />
    <line x1="108" y1="88" x2="108" y2="52" stroke="#FBBF24" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-dasharray="3 3" />
    <text x="112" y="50" font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace" font-size="8" fill="#FBBF24">150</text>
    <line x1="172" y1="88" x2="172" y2="34" stroke="#06B6D4" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-dasharray="3 3" />
    <text x="176" y="32" font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace" font-size="8" fill="#06B6D4">300</text>
    <line x1="228" y1="88" x2="228" y2="16" stroke="#8B5CF6" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-dasharray="3 3" />
    <text x="200" y="12" font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace" font-size="8" fill="#8B5CF6">560</text>
    <g font-family="JetBrains Mono, monospace" font-size="7" fill="#475569">
      <text x="2" y="100">M</text><text x="40" y="100">T</text><text x="78" y="100">W</text>
      <text x="116" y="100">T</text><text x="154" y="100">F</text><text x="192" y="100">S</text>
      <text x="228" y="100">S</text>
    </g>
  </svg>
</SplitCard>

<div class="mt-6"><VideoSlot topic="Weekly Activity Volume" /></div>
<p class="mt-6 text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
  The Weekly Ascent draws no lines to clear and has no ceiling. The
  climb rises as far as your week does, and a flag is planted where it
  passes 150, 300 and 610 measured minutes &mdash; only once passed, so
  there is never a mark ahead of you to fall short of. Someone who runs
  thirty miles every weekend and logs 1,200 minutes sees a climb to 1,200.
  The first two figures are the familiar public-health doses. The third
  is newer, larger, and measured the same way Verve measures you.
</p>
<p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
  <strong class="text-text-primary">The climb is drawn as two bands.</strong> The line is
  the week&rsquo;s measured moderate-plus-vigorous minutes, exactly as before. Beneath it, the
  area is split: moderate minutes fill from the ground up, and vigorous minutes sit on top of
  them, in a darker green. Nothing is re-weighted &mdash; vigorous is not credited double the
  way WHO&rsquo;s moderate-equivalent doses are, because the axis carries measured minutes and
  one axis holds one unit. What the bands add is composition: intensity drives most of the
  fitness benefit, and a 75-minute week that was all hard running now looks like what it is
  rather than like half a target.
</p>
<div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
  {WEEKLY_VOLUME_SECTION.map((c) => <CitationCard {...c} />)}
</div>
